+### `ledDrive` — LED brightness in % (the friendly wrapper over `setAnalogOut`)
+
+`ledDrive` drives an LED through a **BuckPuck constant-current driver** wired to the same
+"Analog Out (0–5V)" BNC (J27 DAC, `SET_AO_VOLTAGE 0xA0`). Instead of asking the author to
+know that the BuckPuck control pin is *inverted* (≈1.65 V = full brightness, ≥4.2 V = off),
+`ledDrive` takes a plain **`percent` 0–100** (% of full light output, `step 0.1`) and the
+**web runner** maps it to the control voltage via a digitized BuckPuck datasheet curve
+before emitting the same `0xA0` frame. `0` → 5000 mV (safely past the shutoff, LED dark),
+`100` → 1650 mV (full). Prefer `ledDrive` for optogenetic/visible-LED intensity so students
+calibrate in %; drop to raw `setAnalogOut mv:` only when you need an exact voltage or a
+non-LED analog device. The curve is approximate (read off the datasheet figure) — for
+photometric work, measure and recalibrate. Like the other two, it's **G6-only** and
+instantaneous. (Background: this is the "LED_AO_drive" capability added 2026-07 for the
+course rigs.)
